message: "If you use this software or data, please cite it as below."
title: "NCQC: Network-Constrained Quality Control for river discharge records (Mackenzie–Liard confluence, 2000–2026)"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: 2026-10-25
license: MIT
authors:
  - family-names: Razavi
    given-names: Hooman
keywords:
  - hydrometry
  - streamflow
  - quality control
  - data reliability
  - mass balance
  - Mackenzie River
repository-code: "https://github.com/<github-user>/ncqc-mackenzie-liard"
abstract: >-
  Code and data for a network-constrained quality-control framework (NCQC) that
  uses mass-balance redundancy among hydrometric gauges to detect, attribute and
  assess inconsistencies in published discharge records, demonstrated for three
  Water Survey of Canada stations at the Mackenzie–Liard confluence.
